 "relevance_note": "Single case report of a woman with a diagnosis of Blau syndrome (\"A 52-year-old woman with Blau syndrome\"); in scope by diagnosis, although no NOD2 testing or variant is reported.",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; no script transcription of tables. One individual, labelled 'patient' (rule 5). The paper reports no NOD2 testing and prints no variant, so the variants table is empty; the diagnosis basis is not stated. Age 52 is taken as age at report; the abstract's '52-year-old woman was diagnosed with Blau syndrome' could be read as age at diagnosis, but she was treated for it from 2006, so age at diagnosis is left not reported. Statements that Blau syndrome is 'characterized by skin rash, uveitis, and rheumatoid arthritis' describe the disease, not this patient, and were not used. 'Rheumatoid arthritis' (a co-diagnosis) was used for the checklist item arthritis. 'Erythema tuberculatum' was mapped to skin rash, not to erythema nodosum. AKI (attributed by the authors to mizoribine-induced hyperuricemia) was recorded under the checklist item 'granulomatous nephritis or renal failure' as renal failure. Table 1 laboratory values (e.g. Hb 8.5, RF 82.7, ANA x40) were not turned into features unless the text interprets them. Vital status 'alive' from the statement that she recovered and was discharged. No contradictions found.",
